---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Work with me" description="Martin Swinkels is a freelance DevOps engineer for Azure platforms, pipelines and Microsoft 365 automation, working remotely from Portugal.">
  <div class="hero single">
    <div>
      <div class="eyebrow">Freelance &middot; 1 to 3 days a week &middot; Remote from Portugal</div>
      <h1>Platforms your teams can <em>deploy to without asking</em>.</h1>
      <p class="lede">I set up Azure and delivery pipelines so they are repeatable, governed and documented, then hand them over or keep improving them with your team.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section>
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h2>What I help with</h2>
      <div class="work-grid">
        <article><h3>Azure landing zones</h3><p>Management groups, policy, naming and diagnostics, defined in Bicep and deployed through reviewed pull requests.</p><div class="chips"><span>Bicep</span><span>Policy</span><span>Governance</span></div></article>
        <article><h3>Pipelines and platforms</h3><p>CI/CD on GitHub Actions and Azure DevOps, with environments and passwordless sign-in to Azure through OIDC.</p><div class="chips"><span>GitHub Actions</span><span>Azure DevOps</span><span>OIDC</span></div></article>
        <article><h3>Microsoft 365 automation</h3><p>SharePoint, Teams and Entra ID configured from definition files, so a tenant can be rebuilt and audited.</p><div class="chips"><span>PnP PowerShell</span><span>Graph</span><span>Entra ID</span></div></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h2>How we work</h2>
      <ul class="now">
        <li><span class="tag">About 3 months</span><div><h3>A defined result</h3><p>A landing zone, a pipeline foundation or a tenant automation, delivered with code, documentation and a handover.</p></div></li>
        <li><span class="tag">Up to 2 years</span><div><h3>Part of your team</h3><p>A steady platform or DevOps engineer for one to three days a week, working in your backlog and your repositories.</p></div></li>
        <li><span class="tag">As needed</span><div><h3>Review and advice</h3><p>A second pair of eyes on a design, a pipeline or a deployment approach before you commit to it.</p></div></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h2>Practical</h2>
      <ul class="now">
        <li><span class="tag">Availability</span><div><p>One to three days a week.</p></div></li>
        <li><span class="tag">Location</span><div><p>Remote from the Algarve, Portugal, one hour behind the Netherlands. On site by arrangement.</p></div></li>
        <li><span class="tag">Languages</span><div><p>Dutch, English and German.</p></div></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h2>Worked example</h2>
      <div class="kite">
        <div>
          <div class="eyebrow">MSCKite</div>
          <h3>Azure Platform Kite</h3>
          <p>My own toolkit for governed Azure delivery. It is being rolled out at a start-up and its customers, which is where I learn what works in practice.</p>
          <p style="margin:0"><a class="more" href="https://github.com/msckite/az-platform-kite" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">github.com/msckite/az-platform-kite &rarr;</a></p>
        </div>
        <img class="mark" src="/msckite-logo.png" width="800" height="540" alt="MSCKite logo" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <div class="contact">
        <p>Tell me what you are building and when you need help.</p>
        <p class="meta" style="font-size:15px">Use LinkedIn, Bluesky or GitHub in the footer below.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
